WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.102
Welcome, everybody, welcome.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.602
Please enjoy yourself.
Welcome. Thank you.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:06.873
Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.976
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.378
Happy Friday, everyone.
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.313
Now, let's get to
some news here.

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:17.383
Well, we've all gotten used to
wearing masks wherever we go,

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.453
but I just read that
the CDC is looking into

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.156
whether it's still necessary
to wear them outdoors.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.425
-Oh?
-Ohh.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.227
-That's all this country
needs right now --

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.195
Trevor,
the bartender from Señor Frog's,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.563
to have been right all along.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.365
He's like, "I told you, bro!"

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.600
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.035
I guess this is good,

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.804
although I was kind of looking
forward to another summer

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.606
with bikini lines on my face,
you know?

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:40.807
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.709
-Honestly,
it would be nice to get back to

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.377
when a masked man
outside your house

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.778
was just a serial killer,
you know?

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.613
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.982
Well, guys, it's a big weekend
for Hollywood.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:52.752
The 93rd annual Oscars
are this Sunday.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.454
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.856
Yeah.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.126
Of course, in quarantine, even
the Oscar statue gained weight.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.895
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.731
Yeah, it's gonna be a very
unique year for the Oscars.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.601
There's no host, no after party,
and no movies anyone saw.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.004
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.139
-Yep, this year's Oscars
are about celebrating

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.041
all the movies
we scrolled through and thought,

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.809
"20 bucks? Nope."

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.211
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.279
But this is interesting --
the Academy announced

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:23.649
that masks are not required
while cameras are rolling,

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.718
but should be worn
during commercial breaks.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.353
-Huh?
-Huh?

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.455
-That makes sense.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.790
-If we've learned anything
about the virus,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.959
it -- it only spreads
during commercials.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.861
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.030
And speaking of movies, today,
"Mortal Kombat" was released

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.832
in theaters and on HBO Max.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.767
I haven't seen
the new "Mortal Kombat" yet,

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.703
but I think I speak
for everyone when I say

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.872
I just hope
it lives up to the play.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.874
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.677
Hey, check this out -- Netflix
is reportedly nearing a deal

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:53.446
on an upcoming biopic
about the band KISS,

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.515
called "Shout It Out Loud."

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.050
Yeah, it's pretty exciting news.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.252
-[ Chuckling ]
Yeah, Jimmy, so exciting.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.653
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:05.024
-Higgins, I didn't realize
you were such a big KISS fan.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.126
-What? No, no, no.
I just love biopics.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.795
[ Light laughter ]
-I-I see.

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.330
Did you know in advance
that I'd be talking

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.232
about a KISS biopic today?

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.833
-No. Just took a chance.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:18.571
I wear KISS makeup to work
about half the time.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.839
-All right. Well, you --

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.408
you can't wear that
during the show.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.043
-Ugh.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.478
Fine.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.913
You never support me, anyway.

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:29.248
-Oh, come on.
I -- Thanks, buddy.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.784
I-I appreciate it.
-Oh, you know what?

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.321
It's me. I'm sorry...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.189
-Yeah.
Get this --

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:40.393
starting on May 1st,
topless clubs in Las Vegas

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.061
are officially allowed
to reopen.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.263
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.931
Whew!

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.432
Just in time for Mother's Day,
you know?

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.933
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:50.102
If you're excited
about topless clubs reopening,

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.105
I'm assuming
it was a long quarantine.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.372
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.508
Listen to this --
Nathan's is offering

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.544
5-cent hot dogs at Coney Island
this summer

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.513
for the first time in 100 years.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:03.716
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.718
[ Applause ]

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.452
Customers were like,
"Uh, I'd actually feel better

00:03:07.452 --> 00:03:08.855
if you charged more."

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.123
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.858
5-cent hot dogs?

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.127
I'd rather get
5-cent LASIK eye surgery.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.161
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.195
What?

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.097
Eating a 5-cent hot dog
is as safe

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.700
as taking home a mattress
on the street that says, "Free."

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.970
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.672
"Seems like a good deal."
-"Hey. Yeah."

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:26.873
-"Let's take it
back to the house."

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.074
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.975
Oh, I saw that Martha Stewart
just announced

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:31.811
the release
of her 99th cookbook.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.212
-Whoo!
-Oh.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:34.914
-99.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.182
At this point,
the recipes are just...

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.820
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Rude.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.055
-It says, "Leave me alone,"
in the book.

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.924
-Wow.
Very rude for a cookbook.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.859
-She would never.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.060
Did you guys hear about this?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.997
An explosion
at a gender-reveal party --

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.631
my gosh --
in New Hampshire

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:55.701
was so powerful that it damaged
[Chuckling] nearby homes

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.003
and was felt in other states.

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.272
-What?
-What?

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.773
Now, what's up with
these gender-reveal parties?

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.642
-Like...
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.543
After the explosion,
everyone was like,

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:06.279
"It's a...lawsuit!"

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.814
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.115
What is going on
with these things?

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:11.417
-It's crazy.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.851
They're supposed to reveal
the gender of the baby,

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:14.486
not the IQ of the parent.

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:17.390
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.325
-Well, this made me laugh --
a man in Taiwan

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.527
is making news for finding
an interesting way

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.495
to get some extra time off
from work.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:24.731
Listen to this story.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:27.233
-A man in Taiwan found
a creative way

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:30.136
to get an extended vacation
from work.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.305
He initially got married
last April.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.106
He was given eight days off.

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:37.309
At the end of his leave,
he divorced his wife

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:39.778
and planned to remarry her
the next day.

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:43.149
And he did this whole process
not once, not twice,

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.517
but three times.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.318
-[ Laughing ] Wow.

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:47.653
Wow! Yeah.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:48.955
His boss knew something was up

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.423
when he got a letter
that said...

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.693
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:56.329
And, finally,
a woman here in New York City

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.065
came home to her apartment
and found an unexpected visitor.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.132
Watch this.

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:09.308
♪♪

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:11.310
[ Audience groans ]
-What?!

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.213
-Wow. I didn't even know
New York City pigeons laid eggs.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:15.648
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.683
I thought they were just rats
that earned their wings.

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.719
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.290
Don't worry, though --
the pigeon's gone,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.093
and this is
no relation at all --

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.594
I just want to remind everyone

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.764
about Nathan's 5-cent hot dogs
this summer on Coney Island.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:32.899
Happy summer, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

